WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:03.730
Get ready for one of those big, "Oh, yeah!"
moments.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:08.149
You know him as a robot on a bloody quest
for vengeance in a genre-defining show -- and

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:09.310
so much more.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:10.500
Keep watching!

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.400
Disney has another big win on its hands with
Hawkeye, the most recent show in the Marvel

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.910
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:20.750
The series stars Hailee Steinfeld as future
Young Avenger Kate Bishop, a maverick archer

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:26.060
who joins up with Clint Barton to take down
the Tracksuit Mafia and their leader, Echo.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.540
Also known as Maya Lopez, Echo is depicted
as a deaf antagonist looking to avenge the

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.110
death of her father, who Clint killed during
his time as vigilante Ronin.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.760
Part of Hawkeye's third episode tells Maya's
origin story, detailing the events of her

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.760
early life.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.350
This plotline also introduces her father,
William Lopez, and the reason for Maya's dogged

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.260
pursuit of Clint and Kate.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:54.640
"You have to learn to jump between two worlds."

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.359
Though William's time on Hawkeye is fleeting,
viewers may just recognize the actor who plays

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.359
him.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:04.660
Zahn McClarnon has had roles in movies and
television since the late '80s, but one of

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.630
his most recognizable parts is that of Officer
Mathias on Longmire.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:13.020
This series is a modern Western that follows
Sheriff Longmire and his attempt to solve

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.790
crimes in Wyoming after the death of his wife.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:20.720
A&amp;E canceled after only three seasons but
was picked up by Netflix, though it was eventually

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.810
canned after three more seasons.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:26.620
McClarnon's Officer Mathias appeared as a
foil to Longmire on the show.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.950
As the chief of police for the Cheyenne reservation,
Mathias' professional interests are often

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.030
at odds with Longmire.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.970
As an Indigenous actor, McClarnon's casting
gave a relevance to the series that depicted

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.770
the lives of Native people.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:44.520
Not long after he exited Longmire, McClarnon
joined the cast of Westworld, beginning with

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.720
the Season 2 episode, "Reunion."

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:52.770
This HBO series is an update of the 1973 film
of the same name, in which robots at a futuristic

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.280
theme park gain sentience and overthrow their
oppressors.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.180
In Season 2 of Westworld, Dolores becomes
the leader of the robot resistance.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.750
However, this narrative encounters a somewhat
confusing plot twist when Native American

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.220
robot Akecheta enters the show.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:11.690
Akecheta is the leader of the Ghost Nation,
having been created to act as a villain for

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.560
a violent narrative in the park.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.450
As it turns out, Akecheta actually became
self-aware years before Dolores and the other

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:19.450
hosts.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.190
McClarnon's portrayal as the Westworld Host
is incredibly nuanced, and he gives an amazing

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.260
and heartfelt performance in the role.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:29.780
As Akecheta, he struggles with his consciousness,
determined to lead his compatriots into a

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:30.780
new world.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:35.590
Soon after Westworld, Zahn McClarnon featured
in the 2019 horror movie Doctor Sleep.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:40.030
In this adaptation of the Stephen King novel,
McClarnon depicts a villainous character named

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.030
Crow Daddy.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:45.620
Both he and the film's lead antagonist Rose
the Hat encounter Danny Torrance as they attempt

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.460
to hunt down a powerful young girl named Abra,
in the hopes of feeding on her ability to

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.680
"shine."

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.540
Rose the Hat, Crow Daddy, and the rest of
their cult are established as antagonists

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.320
with no redeeming qualities.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:01.870
They survive only off of the death of innocents
and, as a result, suffer the consequences

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.819
at the hands of Danny and Abra.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:08.180
Crow Daddy obviously doesn't live to see the
end of the film, but McClarnon nevertheless

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.920
used the role to prove that he can play one
heck of a villain.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.400
In Zahn McClarnon's most recent television
credit before Hawkeye, the actor demonstrated

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.070
his comedic chops on the FX series Reservation
Dogs.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:23.730
Created by Taika Waititi, the show is a candid
depiction of teenagers living on a reservation

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.720
in present-day Oklahoma.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:30.069
Over the course of the show's first season,
viewers follow four kids who dream of escaping

00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:35.400
the confines of the reservation, committing
petty crimes to fund their eventual getaway.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:40.500
McClarnon appears in four episodes of the
show's first season as Big, a noble, but sometimes

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.930
oblivious, reservation police officer.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:46.890
The actor doesn't often get to play to the
funnier side of things during his roles, but

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.260
his character here is a welcome source of
levity on a show that, at times, can actually

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.650
be kinda bleak.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:57.140
Thankfully, Reservation Dogs has been renewed
for a Season 2 — so McClarnon is likely

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:01.420
to reprise his role sometime in the near future.

